[# docs-src/repos/cx-binding-go.cxd — the Go binding's page,
   repo-cx-binding-go.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 4).
   Facts from the registries; the one example from the front door's ABI
   vectors, the corpus the binding's own lane grades itself against. #]

[repo name=cx-binding-go
  [intro
    """**TL;DR — the same C ABI, in the host's own idiom.** `cx-binding-go`
       is `cxlib` as a Go module: a thin wrapper over `libcx`'s string-in,
       string-out C ABI, so a Go program parses, canonicalises, hashes,
       converts and evaluates CX with the very engine the `cx` binary runs —
       byte-identical answers, nothing reimplemented."""]
  [body
    """Layer 1 is the contract every binding shares: sixteen canonical
       methods — parse, bytes, hash, equals, eval, select, modify and the
       node accessors — with identical semantics across hosts, so a document
       hashed from Go is the document hashed from anywhere else. Identity
       rides `cx_canonical`, `cx_hash` and `cx_eq`; selection, evaluation and
       update delegate to `cx_code_eval`; nothing about a document is
       retained inside `libcx` between calls. [[layer-1]] is the table,
       [[c-abi]] the surface beneath it, [[layer-2]] the host-idiomatic
       sugar above it that desugars to Layer 1."""]
  [body
    """We grade the binding against the front door's published ABI vectors —
       one case per entry point a wrapper covers, an input document and the
       canonical output, hash or refusal it must answer — through the
       binding's own lane, written in Go, which loads the file from its pin
       and asserts every vector through its own wrapper. The same file is
       checked against `libcx` directly by the front door's C test, so the
       wrapper and the engine are held to one witness."""]
  [gives
    """No CX module: a binding ships host code, not `.cx` files, so the table
       below is the generator's note. What it gives you is the Go module
       itself — the Layer-1 methods, and the package-level conveniences that
       desugar to them."""]
  [try
    """One ABI vector, replayed by this site's `cx`: an XML document imported
       to CX through the entry point the wrapper's `XmlToCx` calls, and the
       canonical text it must answer. The binding's lane asserts the same
       vector through the wrapper; this page shows the engine's own answer."""]
  [fixture id=abi-010-xml-to-cx]
  [status
    """The binding is not consumed by `cx` — it consumes `cx`: its own
       `deps.cxd` pins the front door for the C ABI and the V core it builds
       `libcx` from, which is why the registry row carries no `at=` and the
       figure draws no column on either side. It ships from its own
       repository at its own cadence, and a pin moves there only when the
       newer front door is green with it."""]]
